      "id": "ES-C381-saltar",
      "sequence": 7990,
      "title": "saltar — a jump over the top",
      "headword": "saltar",
      "romanization": "saltar",
      "gloss": "to jump — Latin saltare, and the somersault is a jump over the top",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:5eb8f05b473ffc93",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say to break. (Romper.) And to wash? (Lavar.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know first",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "el pie — what you jump with."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "arriba — where you jump to."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "pronunciation",
          "title": "Sounds you'll need",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "sal-TAR, two beats with the weight on the second. The l is clear, never swallowed the way English swallows it in salt. see pronunciation reference."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "saltar — \"to jump.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Latin saltare meant to leap, and also to dance — the two were one idea to a Roman. The Spanish is the Latin, so once more the branch is the interesting part."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The best one is somersault, which does not look like it contains a Latin verb at all. It is supra saltus — a jump over the top. The first half is Latin supra, above, the same supra in supranational; the second half is this verb. A somersault is a going-over-jump, and the word has been carrying that description, unread, for centuries."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two more: assault is ad- plus this verb, leaping at somebody. And a sally, when troops rush out of a fort, is the same leap from the French."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The false friend is right there in the pronunciation note: salt is not related. English salt is a native Germanic word, cousin to Latin sal, and has nothing to do with jumping. Salt and somersault only rhyme."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You can now name the action: saltar. And you can take a somersault apart into two Latin words."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "saltar",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *saltar*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "saltar arriba",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *saltar arriba*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "romper",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *romper*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 6,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What are the two halves of somersault? (Supra — above; saltus — a jump.) Is salt related? (No.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
